ailing—maybe 1-2 easy tasks accidentally succeed in 1-2 episodes, but 0-2% success rate is functionally equivalent to complete failure. This rules out the alternative explanation that M=128's compression was too extreme.\n\nNow looking at VTC-only training on OpenVLA across different M values—it fails uniformly regardless of the compression setting. The core issue is that MLP projector tokens lack the spatial entanglement that VTC is designed to solve, so re-encoding them doesn't help; the tokens already have partial independence between them. Looking at the comparison between SmolVLA and OpenVLA across different M values, the data shows a stark contrast—SmolVLA maintains consistent success rates around 56-62% while OpenVLA consistently fails at 0-2%, which visually reinforces that VTR is really a connector-specific solution rather than a universal compression approach. This means I need to narrow Claim 4's scope to pixel-shuffle architectures specifically, though it also highlights a gap: there's no compression solution yet for MLP projectors, which weakens the practical impact. The next step is testing OpenVLA with M=64 using full training over 100K steps to see if we can achieve around 2% success rate. 即使在近似直通的M=96配置下仍然失败，这排除了压缩伪影的可能性，说明VTC模块本身的前向传播就破坏了MLP投影器token的结构。现在看SmolVLA VTR在M=32下的三种随机种子的结果确认，最坏情况下的平均成功率约60%，标准差很小，这些数据已经验证过了。\n\nVTR在像素重排上的有效性是确凿的，这是最坏情况叙述中最强的正面证据。接下来要评估RoboFlamingo使用Perceiver Resampler连接器在LIBERO-Object基准上的表现。\n\n由于CoRL摘要截止仅剩6天，完成100K步的微调、500集评估和剪枝扫描需要2-3天的纯执行时间加上调试，很可能赶不上截止日期。\n\n即使baseline完成了，剪枝扫描也很难在时间内完成。在最坏的情况下，这个实验会被降低优先级——因为收窄后的叙事只需要像素洗牌灾难和线性免疫这两个极端案例，不需要Perceiver Resampler作为第三个连接器族来支撑论点，所以这个实验不是关键的。\n\n现在我需要重新审视用户的要求。他们要求对experiment_plan中每个\"planned\"实验展开详细数据，这可能指的是字面上status为\"planned\"的实验，也可能包括所有还需要结果的实验。看起来应该包括进行中和计划中的实验，因为已完成的实验已经有数据了。\n\n仔细看进行中的实验，c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla大部分评估已完成，剩余的训练运行处于分析状态，评估也都完成了，所以实际上这个已经基本完成。c4_ext_method_universality_openvla确认了M=128是0%，现在在做VTC-only的M=32和M=64训练。c4_ext_openvla_msweep的情况需要继续检查。\n\nd108